<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Andra Markets &middot; FX Analysis &middot; {{ date_long }}</title>
<style>{{ css }}
.kpi{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr); gap:5mm; }
.kpi .stat .v{ font-size:13pt; }
.kpi .stat .c{ font-size:7.4pt; font-weight:600; margin-top:1mm; }
.section.flow{ break-inside:auto; }
.section.flow p, .levels li{ break-inside:avoid; }
.levels{ margin:0; padding-left:4.2mm; }
.levels li{ margin-bottom:1.6mm; }
.legal{ break-inside:avoid; }
</style></head><body>

{% macro tbl(rows, head="Pair") -%}
<table><thead><tr><th>{{ head }}</th><th>Close</th><th>1D</th><th>1W</th><th>1M</th><th>YTD</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in rows %}<tr>
  <td>{{ r.name }}</td>
  <td>{{ r.last | lvl(r.dec) }}</td>
  <td class="{{ r.d1 | dir }}">{{ r.d1 | chg }}</td>
  <td class="{{ r.w1 | dir }}">{{ r.w1 | chg }}</td>
  <td class="{{ r.m1 | dir }}">{{ r.m1 | chg }}</td>
  <td class="{{ r.ytd | dir }}">{{ r.ytd | chg }}</td>
</tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro sec(num, title, note="") -%}
<div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">{{ num }}</span>
  <span class="sec-title">{{ title }}</span>
  {% if note %}<span class="sec-note">{{ note }}</span>{% endif %}</div>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro exh(no, title, img, src) -%}
<figure><div class="ex-head"><div class="ex-no">Exhibit {{ no }}</div>
  <div class="ex-title">{{ title }}</div></div>
  <img src="{{ img }}" alt=""><div class="ex-src">{{ src }}</div></figure>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro prose(id) -%}
{% for p in (n[id] or "").split("\n\n") if p %}<p>{{ p }}</p>{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro %}

<div class="page">
  <div class="rule-top"></div>
  <div class="runhead">
    <div class="mark">Andra Markets</div>
    <div class="runhead-meta">Global Markets Research<br>FX analysis &middot; New York close</div>
  </div>

  <div class="eyebrow"><b>FX Analysis</b><span>{{ date_long }}</span><span>Edition {{ edition }}</span></div>
  <h1>{{ n.headline }}</h1>
  <p class="standfirst">{{ n.standfirst }}</p>
  <div class="byline"><span>Andra Markets Research Desk</span><span>Levels at New York close &middot; Published {{ published }}</span></div>

  <div class="section first">
    <div class="kpi">
      {% for k in kpi %}<div class="stat"><div class="v">{{ k.value }}</div>
        <div class="c {{ k.dir }}">{{ k.chg }}</div><div class="l">{{ k.label }}</div></div>{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    {{ sec("1.0", "Key takeaways") }}
    <div class="g-11">
      <div><ol class="takeaways">{% for k in n.takeaways %}<li>{{ k }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol></div>
      <div>{% if ex.d1 %}{{ exh(1, "Currencies against the dollar, session", ex.d1,
            "Percent. Positive when the currency gained on the dollar. Source: Andra Markets.") }}{% endif %}</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section flow">
    {{ sec("2.0", "The dollar", "Dollar index and the US front end") }}
    <div class="g-11">
      <div>{{ prose("dollar") }}</div>
      <div>{{ tbl(dollar, "Index") }}</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section flow">
    {{ sec("3.0", "G10 majors", "Moves as quoted") }}
    {{ tbl(majors) }}
    <div style="margin-top:3mm">{{ prose("majors") }}</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section flow">
    {{ sec("4.0", "Emerging markets", "Moves as quoted") }}
    {{ tbl(em) }}
    <div style="margin-top:3mm">{{ prose("em") }}</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section flow">
    {{ sec("5.0", "Rate differentials and central banks", "Policy rates, latest published") }}
    {{ prose("drivers") }}
    <div class="g-2" style="margin-top:3mm">
      <div>
        <table><thead><tr><th>Bank</th><th>Rate</th><th>vs Fed</th><th>Last move</th><th>As of</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        {% if fed %}<tr><td>Fed &middot; USD</td>
          <td>{% if fed.rate_lower is not none %}{{ fed.rate_lower | num(2) }}-{% endif %}{{ fed.rate | num(2) }}%</td>
          <td>&middot;</td>
          <td class="{{ fed.last_change_bp | dir }}">{% if fed.last_change_bp is not none %}{{ fed.last_change_bp | bp }}{% else %}n/a{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{{ fed.as_of }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
        {% for b in banks %}<tr><td>{{ b.short }} &middot; {{ b.currency }}</td>
          <td>{{ b.rate | num(2) }}%</td>
          <td>{% if b.vs_fed_bp is not none %}{{ b.vs_fed_bp | bp }}{% else %}n/a{% endif %}</td>
          <td class="{{ b.last_change_bp | dir }}">{% if b.last_change_bp is not none %}{{ b.last_change_bp | bp }}{% else %}n/a{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{{ b.as_of }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="ex-src">Differential to the top of the Fed's target range, basis points.
          Fed and ECB from FRED; other banks from the BIS central bank policy rates
          dataset. As of: date of the latest published observation. Last move: the
          last change in the series.
          {% if banks_without_rate %}No rate available this edition: {{ banks_without_rate | join(", ") }}.{% endif %}</div>
      </div>
      <div>{% if ex.m1 %}{{ exh(2, "Currencies against the dollar, one month", ex.m1,
            "Percent, 21 sessions. Positive when the currency gained on the dollar. Source: Andra Markets.") }}{% endif %}</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section flow">
    {{ sec("6.0", "Levels that matter", "Ranges and moving averages") }}
    <table><thead><tr><th>Pair</th><th>Close</th><th>1M low</th><th>1M high</th><th>50D avg</th><th>200D avg</th><th>52W low</th><th>52W high</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    {% for r in levels %}<tr><td>{{ r.name }}</td><td>{{ r.last | lvl(r.dec) }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.levels.low_1m | lvl(r.dec) }}</td><td>{{ r.levels.high_1m | lvl(r.dec) }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.levels.ma50 | lvl(r.dec) }}</td><td>{{ r.levels.ma200 | lvl(r.dec) }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.levels.low_52w | lvl(r.dec) }}</td><td>{{ r.levels.high_52w | lvl(r.dec) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
    </tbody></table>
    {% if n.levels %}<ul class="levels" style="margin-top:3mm">{% for l in n.levels %}<li>{{ l }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    {{ sec("7.0", "Methodology") }}
    <p style="font-size:6.8pt">Levels are New York closing prints for the session
    shown. Daily, weekly and monthly moves are percent changes over one, five and
    21 sessions, for each pair as quoted: a rise in a USD/XXX pair is a stronger
    dollar, a rise in EUR/USD, GBP/USD, AUD/USD or NZD/USD a weaker one. Exhibits
    show each currency's own move against the dollar. Levels that matter are the
    1-month and 52-week high and low and the 50- and 200-day averages of daily
    closes. Policy rates for the Fed and the ECB are read from FRED and
    those of every other central bank from the BIS central bank policy rates
    dataset, each at its latest published observation, dated in the table.
    Differentials are against the top of the Fed's target range.
    {% if pairs_without_print %} No print this session for {{ pairs_without_print | join(", ") }}.{% endif %}
    Every figure in the text passes the same automated trace check as the daily
    close note before the analysis is released.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="legal">
    <b>Disclaimer.</b> This document is produced by Andra Markets for information
    only. It is not investment advice, a personal recommendation, or an offer or
    solicitation to buy or sell any financial instrument, and it does not take
    account of the objectives, financial situation or needs of any recipient.
    Nothing in it is a forecast or a trade recommendation. Data is drawn from
    sources believed to be reliable; accuracy and completeness are not
    guaranteed. Levels are as of the close shown and may have changed since. Past
    performance does not predict future returns and all investment carries risk
    of loss of capital. No part of this document may be reproduced without
    written permission.
    {% if not audit_ok %}<br><b>Control note.</b> This edition did not fully pass
    the automated figure check. Review the flagged sections before distribution.{% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span>Andra Markets &middot; Global Markets Research</span>
    <span>FX analysis &middot; {{ date_short }}</span><span>Edition {{ edition }}</span></div>
</div>
</body></html>
